{{also|setaside|set-aside}}
==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|sets aside|setting aside|set aside}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[separate]] and [[reserve]] something for a specific [[purpose]].
#: ''Plan to '''set aside''' three or four hours to see the museum.''
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To leave out of account; to omit or neglect.
#* Tillotson
#*: '''Setting aside''' all other considerations, I will endeavour to know the truth, and yield to that.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[disagree]] with something and [[reject]] or [[overturn]] it.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To declare something [[invalid]] or [[null and void]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|fr|put aside}}

